    html: |
      <section class="page-hero" style="background-image:url('assets/img/dest-chengdu.jpg');"><div class="container"><span class="breadcrumb"><a href="index.html">Home</a> &nbsp;/&nbsp; <a href="tours.html">Destinations</a> &nbsp;/&nbsp; Chengdu</span><h1>Chengdu <span class="zh" style="font-family:var(--font-zh);font-size:0.65em;color:var(--gold);">成都</span></h1><p>Chengdu is the capital of easy living — giant pandas snooze in bamboo groves, teahouses spill onto sidewalks, and the air hums with mahjong tiles and the sizzle of Sichuan peppercorns.</p></div></section>
  - label: "Why visit Chengdu?"
    html: |
      <section class="section"><div class="container"><div class="split"><div class="split-media reveal"><img src="assets/img/dest-chengdu.jpg" alt="Chengdu" /><div class="seal-stamp" aria-hidden="true">成<br/>都</div></div><div class="split-copy reveal reveal-d1"><span class="eyebrow">Pandas & Food</span><h2 class="display-h2">Why visit Chengdu?</h2><p>Chengdu is the capital of easy living. Giant pandas snooze in bamboo groves, teahouses spill onto sidewalks, and the air hums with the clatter of mahjong tiles and the sizzle of Sichuan peppercorns. This is the city where China goes to relax — and to eat.</p><p>Between the pandas and the pepper, Chengdu is also the gateway to some of Sichuan's deepest heritage: Taoist mountains, ancient irrigation wonders, and the giant Buddha of Leshan, all within a day trip.</p></div></div></div></section>
  - label: "Chengdu at a glance"
    html: |
      <section class="section" style="padding-top:0;"><div class="container"><div class="stat-strip"><div class="stat-grid" style="grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);"><div class="reveal"><div class="stat-num">80+</div><div class="stat-label">Giant pandas at the Chengdu Research Base — the world's best place to meet them</div></div><div class="reveal reveal-d1"><div class="stat-num">2,300</div><div class="stat-label">Years of city history, from the ancient Shu kingdom onward</div></div><div class="reveal reveal-d2"><div class="stat-num">16M</div><div class="stat-label">Residents make Chengdu a booming southwestern hub</div></div><div class="reveal reveal-d3"><div class="stat-num">No.1</div><div class="stat-label">China's capital of easy living — and of Sichuan cuisine</div></div></div></div></div></section>
  - label: "Iconic experiences in Chengdu"
    html: |
      <section class="section" style="background:var(--white);"><div class="container"><div class="section-head reveal"><span class="eyebrow centered">Must-See Sights</span><h2 class="display-h2">Iconic experiences in Chengdu</h2></div><div class="feature-grid" style="grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);"><div class="card feature-card reveal"><div class="feature-icon"><svg fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M21 10c0 7-9 13-9 13s-9-6-9-13a9 9 0 0 1 18 0z"/><circle cx="12" cy="10" r="3"/></svg></div><h3>Giant Panda Base</h3><p>See giant and red pandas in a lush natural setting. Arrive at 8 AM for feeding time — the cubs are at their most playful.</p></div><div class="card feature-card reveal"><div class="feature-icon"><svg fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M21 10c0 7-9 13-9 13s-9-6-9-13a9 9 0 0 1 18 0z"/><circle cx="12" cy="10" r="3"/></svg></div><h3>Jinli Ancient Street</h3><p>A lively lane of Qing-dynasty architecture, handicraft stalls, and endless Sichuan snacks under red lanterns.</p></div><div class="card feature-card reveal"><div class="feature-icon"><svg fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M21 10c0 7-9 13-9 13s-9-6-9-13a9 9 0 0 1 18 0z"/><circle cx="12" cy="10" r="3"/></svg></div><h3>Wuhou Shrine</h3><p>A serene complex honouring Zhuge Liang, China's most brilliant strategist, set among courtyards and cypress.</p></div><div class="card feature-card reveal"><div class="feature-icon"><svg fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M21 10c0 7-9 13-9 13s-9-6-9-13a9 9 0 0 1 18 0z"/><circle cx="12" cy="10" r="3"/></svg></div><h3>People's Park Teahouse</h3><p>Chengdu's most iconic teahouse — a bamboo chair, a gaiwan of tea, and the slow rhythm of local life.</p></div><div class="card feature-card reveal"><div class="feature-icon"><svg fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M21 10c0 7-9 13-9 13s-9-6-9-13a9 9 0 0 1 18 0z"/><circle cx="12" cy="10" r="3"/></svg></div><h3>Dujiangyan</h3><p>A 2,300-year-old irrigation system still working today — a masterpiece of ancient engineering, 1 h away.</p></div><div class="card feature-card reveal"><div class="feature-icon"><svg fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M21 10c0 7-9 13-9 13s-9-6-9-13a9 9 0 0 1 18 0z"/><circle cx="12" cy="10" r="3"/></svg></div><h3>Kuanzhai Alleys</h3><p>The Wide & Narrow Alleys — restored Qing courtyards now home to teahouses, boutiques and live music.</p></div></div></div></section>
  - label: "The Sichuan Table"
    html: |
      <section class="section"><div class="container"><div class="split"><div class="split-copy reveal"><span class="eyebrow">Food Capital</span><h2 class="display-h2">The Sichuan Table</h2><p>Chengdu is the heart of Sichuan cuisine — the ma-la (numbingly spicy) flavour that has conquered the world. A meal here is a social ritual: hotpot bubbling at the centre of the table, dishes arriving in waves, and tea poured from a long-spouted pot over your shoulder.</p><p>We take you to the back-alley institutions locals actually queue for — not the tourist traps — and tailor the chilli to your comfort level.</p><ul class="tour-highlights" style="grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:10px;"><li><strong>Sichuan hotpot</strong> — a divided red-and-mild pot, the city's communal centrepiece</li><li><strong>Mapo tofu</strong> — silken tofu in a fiery bean-and-chilli sauce</li><li><strong>Dan dan noodles</strong> — sesame, chilli and pork over thin noodles</li><li><strong>Kung pao chicken</strong> — peanuts, dried chilli and a sweet-sour glaze</li><li><strong>Twice-cooked pork</strong> — wok-charred belly with leeks and black beans</li></ul></div><div class="split-media reveal reveal-d1"><img src="assets/img/chengdu-food.jpg" alt="Sichuan hotpot" /><div class="seal-stamp" aria-hidden="true">川<br/>味</div></div></div></div></section>
  - label: "A perfect 4-day journey"
    html: |
      <section class="section" style="background:var(--paper-deep);"><div class="container"><div class="section-head reveal"><span class="eyebrow centered">Sample Itinerary</span><h2 class="display-h2">A perfect 4-day journey</h2><p>Every journey we design is tailor-made — this is a favourite starting point.</p></div><div class="steps-grid" style="grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);gap:22px;"><div class="step reveal"><span class="step-num">01</span><h3>Arrival &amp; Old Lanes</h3><p>Private transfer, settle into a courtyard hotel near Kuanzhai Alleys, then a welcome Sichuan hotpot dinner under the lanterns.</p></div><div class="step reveal reveal-d1"><span class="step-num">02</span><h3>Pandas &amp; Heritage</h3><p>Giant Panda Base at 8 AM, then Wuhou Shrine and Jinli Street, ending with a Sichuan Opera face-changing show.</p></div><div class="step reveal reveal-d2"><span class="step-num">03</span><h3>Ancient Engineering</h3><p>Full-day trip to Dujiangyan's irrigation system and the Taoist summit of Mount Qingcheng — misty, green and peaceful.</p></div><div class="step reveal reveal-d3"><span class="step-num">04</span><h3>Tea &amp; Farewell</h3><p>Morning at the People's Park teahouse, a hands-on hotpot-cooking class for lunch, last shopping, and private airport transfer.</p></div></div></div></section>
  - label: "Chengdu after dark"
    html: |
      <section class="section"><div class="container"><div class="split"><div class="split-media reveal"><img src="assets/img/chengdu-night.jpg" alt="Jinli ancient street at night" /></div><div class="split-copy reveal reveal-d1"><span class="eyebrow">Night Views</span><h2 class="display-h2">Chengdu after dark</h2><p>Chengdu never really sleeps. Teahouses pour late into the night, hotpot restaurants glow with red lanterns, and the bars of Jiuyanqiao spill onto the water. Our evening blends a Sichuan Opera face-changing show with a lantern-lit stroll.</p><ul class="tour-highlights" style="grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:10px;"><li>Sichuan Opera face-changing (bian lian) show with a backstage peek</li><li>Jinli lantern-lit stroll with riverside snacks</li><li>Jiuyanqiao bar street along the Funan River</li><li>Late-night hotpot with the locals</li></ul></div></div></div></section>
  - label: "Beyond the city"
    html: |
      <section class="section" style="background:var(--white);"><div class="container"><div class="section-head reveal"><span class="eyebrow centered">Nearby Escapes</span><h2 class="display-h2">Beyond the city</h2></div><div class="feature-grid" style="grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);"><div class="card feature-card reveal"><div class="feature-icon"><svg fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M21 10c0 7-9 13-9 13s-9-6-9-13a9 9 0 0 1 18 0z"/><circle cx="12" cy="10" r="3"/></svg></div><h3>Leshan Giant Buddha</h3><p>A 71 m Buddha carved into a riverside cliff — so large a person fits inside its toenail. 2 h by high-speed rail.</p></div><div class="card feature-card reveal"><div class="feature-icon"><svg fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M3 18l6-8 4 5 3-4 5 7z"/><path d="M3 21h18"/></svg></div><h3>Mount Emei</h3><p>A sacred Buddhist peak with misty forests, wild monkeys and a sea of clouds at sunrise. Overnight recommended.</p></div><div class="card feature-card reveal"><div class="feature-icon"><svg fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M4 18h16M6 18V8l6-4 6 4v10"/><path d="M10 18v-4h4v4"/></svg></div><h3>Jiuzhaigou</h3><p>Fairy-tale turquoise lakes and tiered waterfalls in a Tibetan-Qiang valley — a flight or scenic drive away.</p></div></div></div></section>
  - label: "Good to know"
    html: |
      <section class="commit-band section"><div class="container"><div class="section-head reveal" style="margin-bottom:20px;"><span class="eyebrow centered">Travel Tips</span><h2 class="display-h2">Good to know before you go</h2></div><div class="commit-grid" style="grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;"><div class="commit-item reveal"><span class="commit-check">✓</span><div><strong>Spice levels</strong><p style="color:rgba(255,255,255,0.72);margin-top:6px;">"Wei la" (mild) to "zhong la" (medium) — we brief every restaurant so the ma-la stays enjoyable, not overwhelming.</p></div></div><div class="commit-item reveal"><span class="commit-check">✓</span><div><strong>Panda timing</strong><p style="color:rgba(255,255,255,0.72);margin-top:6px;">Arrive at the Research Base by 8 AM — that's feeding time and when the cubs are most active and playful.</p></div></div><div class="commit-item reveal"><span class="commit-check">✓</span><div><strong>Weather</strong><p style="color:rgba(255,255,255,0.72);margin-top:6px;">Chengdu is famously overcast and humid. Pack light layers and lean into the teahouse rhythm — it's part of the charm.</p></div></div><div class="commit-item reveal"><span class="commit-check">✓</span><div><strong>Getting around</strong><p style="color:rgba(255,255,255,0.72);margin-top:6px;">The metro is new and spotless; for Dujiangyan and Emei we always arrange a private car and driver for the day.</p></div></div></div></div></section>
